{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Energy cannot be created or destroyed. It can be transferred between stores by mechanical work, electrical work, heating or radiation. In a closed system, no energy is transferred into or out of the system, so the total energy remains constant. Be careful: in thermodynamics, a closed system may exchange energy but not matter with its surroundings. For GCSE energy-conservation questions, the important condition is that no energy crosses the boundary of the system when we claim its total energy stays constant; this is more precisely an isolated system.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 35.928, "words": [["Energy", 0.102083], ["cannot", 0.570833], ["be", 0.922416], ["created", 1.052625], ["or", 1.495333], ["destroyed.", 1.664583], ["It", 3.177083], ["can", 3.398458], ["be", 3.606791], ["transferred", 3.723958], ["between", 4.21875], ["stores", 4.544291], ["by", 4.908875], ["mechanical", 5.039083], ["work,", 5.598958], ["electrical", 6.119791], ["work,", 6.679708], ["heating", 7.161458], ["or", 7.65625], ["radiation.", 7.7995], ["In", 9.322916], ["a", 9.479166], ["closed", 9.622416], ["system,", 9.908875], ["no", 10.651041], ["energy", 10.898458], ["is", 11.328125], ["transferred", 11.497416], ["into", 11.966166], ["or", 12.304708], ["out", 12.487], ["of", 12.669291], ["the", 12.7995], ["system,", 12.890625], ["so", 13.58075], ["the", 13.776041], ["total", 13.90625], ["energy", 14.257833], ["remains", 14.635416], ["constant.", 15.039083], ["Be", 16.614583], ["careful:", 16.835958], ["in", 17.539083], ["thermodynamics,", 17.734375], ["a", 18.789083], ["closed", 18.945333], ["system", 19.166666], ["may", 19.583333], ["exchange", 19.778666], ["energy", 20.260416], ["but", 20.716166], ["not", 20.885416], ["matter", 21.158875], ["with", 21.510416], ["its", 21.679708], ["surroundings.", 21.809916], ["For", 23.502625], ["GCSE", 23.789083], ["energy-conservation", 24.401041], ["questions,", 25.455